> It is also a way to get samples of most scrolls, wands, rings etc so
> you can identify many at once without carrying them around.

And that's what i do "serious" polypiling for - when short on magical
supplies, i generally go and polypile rings, books and scrolls in
hopes of getting more useful stuff. I don't find wands and potions
particularly valuable - wands lose charges when 'morphed, and later in
the game, the only potions i care about are clear ones, and there are
much easier ways of getting those than polymorph.

Polypiling is also a means of keeping your sanity intact when playing
an extinctionist - when the junk has piled up too high, filter out the
few useful items and make some golems. Also useful to get rid of
boulders left behind by giants, particularly when create monster pulls
up both giants and nymphs ...

